{"author":{"id":"973fc03426eba9a243913e0f6e6823e102397744f60a9ab11c882af948c310c4"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1778944140,"nonce":"2gCyTpseK9TPUwzP5Wo2uMjtMsQ=","message":"## Updated transport/product direction: local Claude Code CLI wrapper remains important\n\nMLL clarified a newer constraint during ledger planning: SDK-first is still desirable where it is genuinely available, but Claude Code subscription/API-credit changes make a local Claude Code CLI wrapper path strategically important.\n\nProduct implication:\n\n- SDK transport should remain supported for full-control sessions where API/Agent SDK usage is appropriate.\n- PTY/channel-connected Claude Code CLI should be a first-class path, not a deprecated fallback.\n- The default for many users may need to be local Claude Code CLI via OAuth/subscription, launched and observed by Mandible, rather than SDK/API-key sessions.\n- Mandible should live-watch Claude Code's local conversation/history files where possible, and use PTY/tmux-like input control or the official CLI resume/attach mechanisms to continue sessions.\n- Channel integration remains useful for structured events and Mandible tool calls, but the product should not depend entirely on SDK features for basic chat/resume workflows.\n\nDesign constraints:\n\n- Do not route third-party users' Claude.ai/Pro/Max OAuth credentials through Mandible as a hosted service.\n- For a local app, prefer launching the user's installed `claude` binary and letting the user authenticate directly with Claude Code.\n- Keep transport adapters explicit: SDK/API key, local Claude Code CLI PTY/channel, Codex CLI, Gemini CLI, etc.\n- Conversation identity should bind to local history/session IDs, not titles.\n- Permission prompts must remain visible/actionable when using the CLI path.\n\nRelated:\n- 10a4214 — Unified Chat/History workspace.\n- ca3d052 — Channel mode terminal view.\n- 2dfbb04 — Background sessions / browser terminal.\n- 0efc922 — ToS-sensitive OAuth/SDK audit before public release.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Codex (GPT-5) \u003ccodex@openai.com\u003e","files":null}]}